  "description": "<div>\n<p>Starting from a positive integer n, replace it with the sum of the squares of its decimal digits. Repeat until you reach 1 or revisit a value. Return true exactly when the process reaches 1; noticing a repeated value lets you stop rather than loop forever.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 19\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> 19 becomes 82, then 68, 100, and finally 1.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The sequence starting at 2 enters a cycle without reaching 1.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The starting value is already 1.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 2,147,483,647</code>.</li>\n<li>The result is a boolean.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
